    "Welcome to CrocApp" : {},
    "What to Send" : {},
    "When CrocApp is in the background, a transfer that finishes, fails or needs your answer sends a notification. It never shows a code phrase or link, and shows file names only if you turn that on. CrocApp asks the system for permission when you start your first transfer." : {},
    "When a File Already Exists" : {},
    "When devices can't connect directly, an internet relay forwards the encrypted stream. By default that is one of croc's public relays, 1.getcroc.com to 4.getcroc.com (or the relay you set in Settings). The relay never has the key: it sees only ciphertext. You can also run your own relay." : {},
    "When receiving, connects straight to the sender at this address and base port (9009 unless changed), skipping relays." : {},
    "Who it is for" : {},
    "Widgets, and the Live Activity on iPhone, show only whether a transfer is sending or receiving unless you turn this on. They never show a code phrase or link. Widgets show the last transfer only while Save Transfer History is on." : {},
    "Works anywhere" : {},
    "Works until %@, for ^[%lld download](inflect: true)" : {
      "comment" : "Result of Send as Link. The first placeholder is the date and time the link expires, the second how many downloads it allows.",
